    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίβυλλ-α</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ἡ</span>, <u>Sibyl</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Heraclit.
			92
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Pax</u>
			1095
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			1116
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Phdr.</u>
			244b
		</span></i>. Early writers only recognize <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one</i> Sibyl (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίβυλλαι καὶ
				Βάκιδες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				954a36
			</span></i>, is no exception), first localized at Erythrae or Cumae,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				838a6
			</span></i>; later, others are mentioned, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.1.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				10.12.1
			</span></i> sqq., Sch.Pl.l.c., Buresch <i><span class="en">
				<u>Klaros</u>
				p.120
			</span></i>. [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίβιλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1534.85
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>.]</div>
